            <ArticleTitle>Life-threatening glossopharyngeal neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>660-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Glossopharyngeal neuralgia is a rare condition that, on occasions, may be associated with cardiac dysrhythmia. This case report describes the case of an 86-year-old woman whose glossopharyngeal neuralgia was complicated by life-threatening dysrhythmias and who was cured by posterior fossa rhizotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
